    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-12838",
      "problem": "Consider the hexagon shown below. Draw an exterior angle of $\\angle B.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14193271/assets/fc1834e88b4d08a2705059d28d21105047898f251f0f2c29f8509be7b6321de0.png)",
      "worked_solution": "To construct an exterior angle of $\\angle B,$ we extend $\\overline{AB}$ past $B.$ The angle between $\\overline{BC}$ and the extension of $\\overline{AB}$ is an exterior angle of $\\angle B.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14193271/assets/d91fc772042490e0785a4a617e4c3785c8616b7ed0ff05509ca8bc902eccc2a8.png)\n\nAnother way to construct an exterior angle of $\\angle B$ is to extend $\\overline{CB}$ past $B.$ The angle between $\\overline{AB}$ and the extension of $\\overline{CB}$ is also an exterior angle of $\\angle B.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14193271/assets/8d031a6a6cc1513fc0a8031755b537d144279b88c964fc75728d3588ae1e4af9.png)",
